// What the checker records for an editor (todo.md, Language server), as `ctxc decls` prints it.
// A const's binders have theirs too; a body with errors still records what it declared.
//# build text: {home}/tests/helpers/text.ctx

// `ctxc decls` prints std's declarations too, thousands of lines that change with std, so the
// output isn't stated whole: its `live` lines are these, in a row,
//# $ ctxc decls {std:abs} -- main.ctx
//# stdout has:
//|
//| live x i32 main.ctx:2:48-2:53
//| live z {error} main.ctx:5:17-8:2
//| live w i32 main.ctx:6:14-8:2
//|

// and it has no other line that starts with `live `.
//# $ {text} to out.txt {ctxc} decls {std:abs} -- main.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# $ {text} count out.txt "\nlive "
//# stdout:
//| 3
